<title>TURKEY: TABLE - Turk paint firm Marshall H1 net profits jump.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Turk paint firm Marshall H1 net profits jump.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 1,502.71  vs     608.45</p>
<p>    Net profit		  1,084.36  vs     439.06</p>
<p>    Net sales		   8,751.79  vs   4,446.38</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  1,859.37  vs     741.80</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  245.44  vs	91.26</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 249.61  vs	85.99</p>
<p>    Total debts		 3,951.06  vs   1,820.59</p>
<p>    Equity			5,376.58  vs   2,485.06</p>
<p>    Capital			 721.60  vs     721.60</p>
<p>NOTE - Shares of Turkish paint and varnish producer Marshall Boya ve Vernik Sanayii AS are also listed on the Munich bourse.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
